    {
      "name": "Verify NotificationLog After Celery Fires",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": ""
        },
        "description": "### Test 13: Verify NotificationLog After Celery Fires\n\n**Purpose:** Verify that the Celery notification task creates a `NotificationLog` record.\n\n**Procedure:**\n\n1. Start the Celery worker.\n    \n2. Trigger `check_prices`.\n    \n3. Wait for the worker to process the task.\n    \n4. Inspect the database using the Django shell:\n    \n\n```\nfrom pulse.models import NotificationLog\nprint(\"Total logs:\", NotificationLog.objects.count())\nprint(list(NotificationLog.objects.values()))\n\n ```\n\n**Expected result:** A matching `NotificationLog` record exists when an active alert meets its trigger condition and the notification task succeeds.\n\n**Verification method:** Manual database verification; this is not a direct HTTP API request."
      },
      "response": []
    }
